Dear Mark;
      Because of the excitement of the wedding we almost forgot to wish you a
Happy Birthday.  We also send you and Sukran All of our Love.   Dad and Mother

I will be passing out ETS' (mailing Omaha's to Ann for distribution) updated wallet-size phone list.  The list includes blackberry numbers.

Below, please find directions to set your blackberrys to be notified of only high priority messages.  All other messages will reach your blackberry, but you will not be disturbed by routine messages.  A person notifying you will have to indicate that the message is high priority.  If you have any problems, let me know.

1.	Run the Desktop Manager;
2.	Double click on Redirector Settings;
3.	Select the Filters tab;
4.	Select New;
5.	Type a filter name (whatever you makeup for this exercise), click on Importance and change drop down box to High.  Click the box Forward with Level 1 Notification;
6.	Click ok, apply, ok;
7.	Now go to the handheld device and choose Options.  Choose Notify, then move down to Level 1 Notify Only and make sure it indicates Yes.

Iris S. Waser
Enron Transportation Services Company
1400 Smith Street, EB 4749b
Houston, TX  77002
713-853-6059
713-853-5425 - fax
iris.waser@enron.com

Kim, Patti, Suzanne, and Ted-

The total burn nomination for month of December 2001 is 6,500MMBtu per day.  This is made up of the sum of the following:

1. 3,989MMBtu/day purchase from Engage @ SoCal Border (net, after PG&ENW losses 4,124MMBtu/day @ Kingsgate);
2. 3,000MMBtu/day APEA gas;
3. 1,000MMBtu/day balance of year strip purchased on behalf of Azusa@ $7.71/MMBtu;
4. 2,000MMBtu/day under two separate fixed contracts of 1,000MMBtu/day each;
5. 500MMBtu/day March 2001 through Feb strip purchased @ $7.63;
6. Saleto Enron at SoCalBorder, 3,989MMBtu/day at $2.68/MMBtu

Line loss on the PG & E line for December 2001 is 2.20%.  We have not sold any of the APEA gas (3,000MMBtu/day) at this time.  However, we are looking into selling it and will notify you if we are successful.

Our Broadway 3 steam plant (65MW) is off line for scheduled maintenance.  We will only have Broadway 2 online on a regular basis.  Our actual usage will probably be about 3,500 to 4,000MMBtu per day, unless the ISO instructs us to put Broadway 1 online.  Should Broadway 1 be called upon, our usage will go up to 6,500MMBtu/day.

If you have any questions, please contact me.

Thanks.

-Steve

